course: dictionary
lesson: 2463
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. «Dark» can mean with little or no light, as in «afraid of the dark». It can mean a deep colour, like dark green. It can also mean sad, scary or bad, as in «a dark story». Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. In «The sky went dark after sunset», the word sunset tells you dark means with no light. In «a dark story», the word story is not about light, so dark must mean sad, scary or bad. Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Phrases use dark too. «In the dark» means not knowing something, so if Sam is kept in the dark, nobody has told him the news. «After dark» means once night has come. Phrases often do not mean just what each word means on its own, so learn them as whole chunks.
fact: Dark means with little or no light, like at night.
fact: A dark colour is deep and close to black, like dark green.
fact: Dark hair, eyes or skin are deep brown or black.
fact: «The dark» is the time or place with no light: «afraid of the dark».
fact: Night happens when our side of the Earth faces away from the sun. As the Earth spins, every place moves from the dark half into the light half and back again, once in 24 hours.
exercise: «Mum switched on the lamp because the room was dark.» What does dark mean here? | A deep blue colour | *With little or no light | Very old | Sad and scary
exercise: «Her hair was dark brown, almost black.» What does dark describe? | Her hair's length | *Her hair's colour | How fast she runs | Her favourite food
exercise: «The story was dark and scary, so Ella closed the book.» What does dark mean here? | *Sad, scary or bad | Full of light | The middle of the day | A dark colour
test: Sam was kept in the dark about the party. What does «in the dark» mean? | Very scared of the night | Very dark blue | *Not knowing about it | Hiding under a blanket
test: «He wore a dark green jumper.» What does dark tell you about the colour? | It is bright yellow | It has spots | *It is deep and close to black | It is see-through
exam: «It was dark by six o'clock in winter.» Which meaning of dark is used here? | Bad luck | Sad and scary | *With little or no light | A deep colour
